<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Bivec raises yr shr, offers scrip div.</title>
<headline>Bivec raises yr shr, offers scrip div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     104.1	 vs  85.8</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)     97.4	 vs  82.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  24.5	 vs  23.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    20.60	vs  16.63</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    41.90	vs  33.44</p>
<p>    Tax			   2.46	vs   2.14</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     1.93	vs   4.24</p>
<p>    Turnover		  122.85	vs 130.75</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 4</p>
<p>on register Oct 18</p>
<p>Full name: Berzack-Illman Investments Corp Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     1.33	  vs 0.71</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had decided to award capitalisation shares to shareholders on register October 18 in the ratio of 1.67 capitalisation shares for every 100 ordinary shares held. Shareholders could elect to receive a cash dividend instead.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
